<title>FRANCE: Details of latest EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Details of latest EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments between July 1 and August 27 of the new 1996/97 (July/June) campaign supplied by member country officials. Since the figures were drawn up, the EU has granted exports of 167,500 tonnes of soft wheat, 234,324 tonnes of barley, 9,622 tonnes of rye and 7,500 tonnes of oats.</p>
<p>Figures ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-------</p>
<p>			     1Jul96 to 27Aug96	1Jul95 to 27Aug95</p>
<p>			EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p> Soft wheat(grain)    432     21	 59    2,011	  595</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	     881    113	  1	779	    0</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain	     211    147	  0	144	    0</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	  11     28	  0	 39	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		 0		   0	  0	    0</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   0		   0	  0	    0</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT   1,535     52	 60    2,973	  595</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	  11		 104	  0	  234</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	   31		   0	  0	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		  0		   0	 21	    0</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     42		 104	 21	  234</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	    1,577     53	164    2,994	  829</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)	233     37	  6	632	   50</p>
